89 #edb/ref 1071 "A sphere has a diameter of $8\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{mm}.$ Find the surface area of the sphere." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573889 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5b24908b-3e08-5600-a3ab-060f182d551c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573889 #edb/ref 1074 "We can calculate the surface area of a sphere using the formula\n\n$$\nS=4\\pi {r}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the radius of the sphere.\n\nSubstituting $r=\\frac{8\\sqrt{3}}{2}=4\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{mm}$ into the formula, we obtain\n\n$$\nS=4\\pi {(4\\sqrt{3})}^{2}=192\\pi \\,{\\text{mm}}^{2}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573891 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186573838 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573891 #edb/ref 1069 "q-108139" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573891 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573891 #edb/ref 1071 "The surface area of a sphere is $144\\pi \\,{\\text{in}}^{2}.$ Find the volume of the sphere." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573891 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "63831384-20c1-5413-ac5c-3dae6cac797c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573891 #edb/ref 1074 "We can calculate the surface area of a sphere using the formula\n\n$$\nS=4\\pi {r}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the radius of the sphere.\n\nSubstituting $S=144\\pi \\,{\\text{in}}^{2}$ into the above formula, we can solve for $r$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & =4\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\ 144\\pi  & =4\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{144\\pi }{4\\pi } & ={r}^{2} \\\\ {r}^{2} & =36 \\\\ r & =6\\,\\text{in}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we  can find the volume of the sphere as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & =\\frac{4}{3}\\pi {r}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\pi (6)^{3} \\\\  & =288\\pi \\,{\\text{in}}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573916 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186573785 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573916 #edb/ref 1069 "q-107931" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573916 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573916 #edb/ref 1071 "A sphere has a surface area of $48\\pi \\,{\\text{in}}^{2}.$ Calculate the diameter of the sphere." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573916 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b71e39cd-1ccd-551f-bcc4-e9f7fe121c87" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573916 #edb/ref 1074 "We can calculate the surface area of a sphere using the formula\n\n$$\nS=4\\pi {r}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the radius of the sphere.\n\nSubstituting $S=48\\pi \\,{\\text{in}}^{2}$ into the formula, we can solve for $r$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & =4\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\ 48\\pi  & =4\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{48\\pi }{4\\pi } & ={r}^{2} \\\\ {r}^{2} & =12 \\\\ r & =\\sqrt{12} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{in}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the diameter is\n\n$$\nd=2r=2\\cdot 2\\sqrt{3}=4\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{in}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573925 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186573792 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573925 #edb/ref 1069 "q-118434" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573925 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573925 #edb/ref 1071 "A sphere has a surface area of $25\\pi \\,{\\text{mm}}^{2}.$ Calculate the diameter of the sphere." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573925 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c989d950-e23f-561f-b2b4-ddaf69734abf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573925 #edb/ref 1074 "We can calculate the surface area of a sphere using the formula\n\n$$\nS=4\\pi {r}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the radius of the sphere.\n\nSubstituting $S=25\\pi \\,{\\text{mm}}^{2}$ into the formula, we can solve for $r$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & =4\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\ 25\\pi  & =4\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{25\\pi }{4\\pi } & ={r}^{2} \\\\ {r}^{2} & =\\frac{25}{4} \\\\ r & =\\sqrt{\\frac{25}{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}\\,\\text{mm}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the diameter is\n\n$$\nd=2r=2\\cdot \\frac{5}{2}=5\\,\\text{mm}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573931 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186573827 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573931 #edb/ref 1069 "q-108136" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573931 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573931 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/ca/ca021f8684431c29f48876fc2a079f9e23931862f37f8f0dd4b1c2f73a87169d.png)\n\nFind the surface area of the sphere above, given that its volume is $\\frac{9}{2}\\pi \\,{\\text{in}}^{3}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573931 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d4951800-9f16-50a9-8666-315cfa908dd9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573931 #edb/ref 1074 "We can find the volume of a sphere using the formula\n\n$$\nV=\\frac{4}{3}\\pi {r}^{3},\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the radius of the sphere.\n\nSubstituting $V=\\frac{9}{2}\\pi \\,{\\text{in}}^{3}$ into the formula, we can solve for $r$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & =\\frac{4}{3}\\pi {r}^{3} \\\\ \\frac{9}{2}\\pi  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\pi {r}^{3} \\\\ \\frac{9\\pi \\cdot 3}{2\\cdot 4\\pi } & ={r}^{3} \\\\ {r}^{3} & =\\frac{27}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{{3}^{3}}{{2}^{3}} \\\\  & ={(\\frac{3}{2})}^{3} \\\\ r & =\\frac{3}{2}\\,\\text{in}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, the surface area of ​​the sphere can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & =4\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\  & =4\\pi {(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2} \\\\  & =9\\pi \\,{\\text{in}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
